        "original_id": "5ac8ed3e-0125-58f6-b0b4-d290ec8ff3f7",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Hudson Austin, Maurice Bishop, Bernard Coard, Eric Gairy\n- Organizations: New Jewel Movement\n- Places: Grenada\n- Roles: chairman, general, politician, leader\n- Events: 13 March 1979 revolution, coup, killing of Maurice Bishop, military government\n\nFacts:\n- On 13 March 1979, the revolution in Grenada removed Eric Gairy from office.\n- Maurice Bishop was a Grenadian politician and the leader of the New Jewel Movement.\n- The New Jewel Movement promoted popular efforts in socio-economic development, education, and Black liberation.\n- Maurice Bishop came to power during the 13 March 1979 revolution in Grenada.\n- Bernard Coard launched a coup within the revolutionary government and held power for three days.\n- General Hudson Austin deposed Bernard Coard after those three days.\n- After the killing of Maurice Bishop, Hudson Austin formed a military government in Grenada with himself as chairman.",
